# Preparing a ceramic slurry (draft)

A slurry recipe is written the way lab protocols often are. A reader works out how much of each
ingredient to weigh.

## The recipe

```symblic
given recipe: Text = """Prepare 200 g of a 40% alumina slurry in deionised water with 1% dispersant."""
define Masses as Record {alumina_g: Number, dispersant_g: Number, water_g: Number}
```

## Weighing

Work out the mass of each ingredient to weigh, in grams.

```symblic
ask masses: Masses "How many grams of alumina, dispersant and water should be weighed?" from recipe
ensure masses.alumina_g + masses.dispersant_g + masses.water_g = 200 else retry because "the slurry weighs 200 g in total".
show masses.
```
